---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import MadeByKaj from '../../../components/MadeByKaj.astro';
import LiveNotebook from '../../../components/live/LiveNotebook.astro';
import CodeBlockWithCopy from '../../../components/live/CodeBlockWithCopy.astro';
import cell1 from '../../../live-examples/skykit/star-metadata-sidecars/cell-1.js?raw';
import cell2 from '../../../live-examples/skykit/star-metadata-sidecars/cell-2.js?raw';
import cell3 from '../../../live-examples/skykit/star-metadata-sidecars/cell-3.js?raw';

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const installCode = `npm install @found-in-space/star-octree-provider@0.2.0-alpha.0 @found-in-space/star-trees@0.2.0-alpha.0 @found-in-space/meta-sidecar-provider@0.2.0-alpha.0`;
const browserImportCode = `import {
  OCTREE_DEFAULT,
  createStarOctreeProviderService,
} from "https://esm.sh/@found-in-space/star-octree-provider@0.2.0-alpha.0?bundle";
import {
  createObserverShellStrategy,
} from "https://esm.sh/@found-in-space/star-trees@0.2.0-alpha.0?bundle";
import {
  createMetaSidecarProviderService,
  deriveMetaSidecarUrlFromRenderUrl,
} from "https://esm.sh/@found-in-space/meta-sidecar-provider@0.2.0-alpha.0?bundle";`;
const importCode = `import {
  OCTREE_DEFAULT,
  createStarOctreeProviderService,
} from '@found-in-space/star-octree-provider';
import {
  createMetaSidecarProviderService,
  deriveMetaSidecarUrlFromRenderUrl,
} from '@found-in-space/meta-sidecar-provider';
import { createObserverShellStrategy } from '@found-in-space/star-trees';`;
const cells = [
	{
		id: 'bootstrap',
		title: '1. Bootstrap the dataset',
		description: 'Read the render dataset id, derive the matching meta sidecar URL, and open a metadata provider.',
		initialCode: cell1,
	},
	{
		id: 'stream',
		title: '2. Stream stars with object refs',
		description: 'Load visible cells with StarObjectRef identity so metadata lookup has a public key.',
		initialCode: cell2,
	},
	{
		id: 'labels',
		title: '3. Fetch labels and cell metadata',
		description: 'Fetch one star metadata row and one full cell metadata sidecar, then format useful labels.',
		initialCode: cell3,
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="Fetch names and labels with sidecars | Found in Space"
	description="Enrich streamed SkyKit stars with metadata sidecars using StarObjectRef identity."
>
	<SiteHeader section="Learn & build" />

	<main class="page page--lesson">
		<header class="lesson-hero">
			<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
				<a href={`${basePath}learn-build/`}>Learn &amp; Build</a>
				<span class="breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
				<a href={`${basePath}learn-build/skykit/`}>SkyKit</a>
				<span class="breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
				<span>Metadata sidecars</span>
			</nav>
			<p class="eyebrow">Lesson 4</p>
			<h1>Fetch names and labels with sidecars</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Keep the render stream compact, then fetch richer catalogue metadata only when your
				app needs labels, hover text, or facts about a selected star.
				This is the same data use-case as Lesson 3, with labels added.
			</p>
		</header>

		<article class="lesson-body prose">
			<section>
				<h2>Learning goal</h2>
				<p>
					The render octree streams positions, magnitudes, temperatures, and optional public
					star refs. Metadata sidecars are separate. Your app bootstraps the render dataset id,
					derives the matching sidecar URL, creates a sidecar provider, and looks up metadata
					by <code>StarObjectRef</code> or by semantic cell ref.
				</p>
				<p>
					The label policy in this lesson follows the same shape used by Star Pilot:
					proper name, Bayer designation plus constellation, Flamsteed plus constellation,
					HD, HIP, Gaia source id, then a cell/ordinal fallback.
				</p>
				<p>
					Those labelled rows are still plain JavaScript objects. You can draw them with
					Canvas, PixiJS, Phaser, SVG, or your own renderer.
				</p>
			</section>
		</article>

		<LiveNotebook
			id="skykit-sidecars"
			title="Resolve sidecar metadata"
			description="Run the cells in order. The final cell fetches one star row and one full cell sidecar."
			cells={cells}
		/>

		<article class="lesson-body prose">
			<section class="callout panel">
				<p class="panel__eyebrow">Things to try</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Change the magnitude limit in cell 2 to stream a different visible set.</li>
					<li>Change which candidate row cell 3 inspects before <code>getMeta()</code>.</li>
					<li>Modify the label formatter order in the shared notebook helper.</li>
					<li>Render extra metadata fields in the final table.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>What changed in the code</h2>
				<p>
					Cell 1 calls <code>ensureBootstrap()</code> on the render provider and requires a
					dataset id. It then derives the sidecar URL from the render octree URL and creates a
					metadata provider with the render dataset id as its parent.
				</p>
				<p>
					Cell 3 uses <code>getMeta(star.ref)</code> for one object and
					<code>getMetaCell(...)</code> for all metadata rows in the same semantic cell. The
					sidecar provider stays schema-neutral; the app decides what a label should be.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="source-panel panel">
				<p class="panel__eyebrow">Source and next steps</p>
				<h2>Star Pilot uses this pattern for hover labels.</h2>
				<p>
					Star Pilot derives the render dataset id, opens the matching generated meta sidecar,
					and uses public <code>StarObjectRef</code> values for lookup. The render stream stays
					compact; metadata is fetched only when labels or richer facts are needed.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><a href="https://github.com/Found-in-Space/skykit" rel="noopener noreferrer">SkyKit repository</a></li>
					<li><a href="https://github.com/Found-in-Space/skykit/tree/main/packages/meta-sidecar-provider" rel="noopener noreferrer">Meta sidecar provider package</a></li>
					<li><a href="https://github.com/Found-in-Space/star-pilot" rel="noopener noreferrer">Star Pilot repository</a></li>
					<li><a href={`${basePath}learn-build/skykit/build-a-star-app/`}>Next: build a small app</a></li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="local-panel panel">
				<h2>Use this in a browser</h2>
				<p>
					For standalone browser examples, use stable, pinned CDN URLs directly. The lesson
					does not introduce version constants or URL helper functions.
				</p>
				<CodeBlockWithCopy code={browserImportCode} label="Browser import" language="js" />

				<h2>Use this locally</h2>
				<p>
					Install the data packages and keep the label formatter in your app. The sidecar
					provider intentionally does not choose display names for you.
				</p>
				<CodeBlockWithCopy code={installCode} label="Install" language="bash" />
				<CodeBlockWithCopy code={importCode} label="Local imports" language="js" />
			</section>
		</article>

		<MadeByKaj />
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page--lesson {
		max-width: 76rem;
	}

	.lesson-hero {
		max-width: 60rem;
		padding: 3.5rem 0 1.5rem;
	}

	.lesson-hero h1 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 4rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		line-height: 1;
		letter-spacing: 0;
	}

	.lesson-body {
		max-width: 54rem;
	}

	.source-panel {
		margin: 2.5rem 0;
	}

	.source-panel h2 {
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	.local-panel {
		margin: 2.5rem 0;
	}

	.local-panel h2 {
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.lesson-hero h1 {
			font-size: 2.75rem;
		}
	}
</style>
